Independent review found a critical defect: q6/handoff explicitly says APC is off, but ar.py's _build_apc_meta_for_cold() returns None directly when self.apc_manager is None. So with APC off, continuous batching won't generate session metadata, _session_checkpoint_column_for_meta/_store_session_snapshot won't run, and X-KV-Checkpoint-Before and session store won't take effect on the actual chat AR path. Please fix this directly, keeping APC unchanged: build minimal session metadata/prefill checkpoint path for session-only requests when APC is off, supporting marker exact boundary and old guard fallback; fork-only must also be able to do independent clone suffix prefill. Add an APC-off generation-level focused test proving marker store/fork lookup executes on the AR path. Then rerun focused + full suite, fix all regressions, and commit a new commit (with Co-Authored-By trailer). Don't start q6/server/real models, don't modify the main directory or apc.py. Provide actual test output when done.
